{
  "about": [
    "HD screen coverage (tools/ci/hd_gates.py --checks coverage). Each screen is opened with its commands in one hidden --exec run at hd_scale 3, after 'setup', and screenshotted.",
    "The measure is the share of 3x3 texel blocks (one 640x400 engine pixel each) that are flat, all nine texels equal: what an upscaled indexed pixel looks like. Lower is more HD.",
    "budgets[profile].screens holds the share measured when the budget was recorded; a screen fails when it rises above that by more than 'tolerance'.",
    "A profile is '<pack>@<renderer>': 'baseline' for the pack --make-pack builds, else the pack folder's name; 'gpu' or 'software'.",
    "Record or lower budgets only with --coverage-update, after looking at the report (build/coverage/coverage.md and its masks/); never raise one without a reason in the commit message."
  ],
  "hd_scale": 3,
  "tolerance": 0.002,
  "setup": [
    "game options set lighting false",
    "restaurant qs 0 0"
  ],
  "screens": [
